  "index_interpretation": "Along every chosen axis each four-component copy has two right-moving and two left-moving channels, hence zero net walk index. The conditional shift is therefore in the balanced class compatible with partitioned local unitaries. A rigid one-way eight-channel translation has nonzero index and is a different target. This classification does not prove that the native LFM action supplies the needed local exchange.",
  "interpretation": "A nearest-neighbor Dirac walk conditionally shifts the +gamma and -gamma channels in opposite edge directions. Each of the two four-component flavor copies contains two forward and two backward channels and is preserved by transport. The two copies therefore are not a leading/trailing pair.",
